  "raw_text": "197\n\nTara papulra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nsomeone who pretends to be important, someone who acts in a proud\n\nor haughty way\n \n/ alguien que pretende ser importante, alguien que actúa de una manera orgullosa o\n\naltiva\n\nTara pulaia l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nway of pretending to be important, way of acting important, self\n-\nimportance,\n\narrogance\n, pride\n \n/ forma de pretender ser\n \nimportante, forma de actuar importante, importancia\n\npersonal, arrogancia\n, orgullo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n05/19\n):\n \nDîa muni man\n \nlukisma Baibil ba tara pulaia l\nâ\nka dukiara aisi ba diara yamni sa?\n \n–\n \nWhy do you\n\nthink what the Bible says about\n \nself\n-\nimportance is good?\n \n/ ¿Por qué crees que lo que dice la Biblia sobre la\n\nimportancia personal es bueno?\n)\n\nTara pulan l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nway of pretending to be important, way of acting important, self\n-\nimportance,\n\narrogance, pride\n \n/ forma de pretender ser\n \nimportante, forma de actuar importante, importancia\n\npersonal, arrogancia, orgullo\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n07/20\n):\n \nFero ba tara pulan lâka brin sakuna ai dara walras kira Gâd kupia lâka aimakbia hilp munan\n\n–\n \nPharaoh had arrogance but unconsciously, he helped fulfill God’s will\n \n/ Faraón tenía arrogancia pero\n\ninconscientemente, ayudó\n \na\n \nque se cumpliera\n \nla voluntad de Dios\n)\n\nPulitik\n \n–\n \npolitics\n \n/ política\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n12/19\n):\n \nPulitik bara war aiklabanka nani ba tilara yawan dimaia apia\n \nsa\n \n–\n \nWe must not get\n \ninvolved in war and\n\npolitics; We must be neutral\n \n/ No debemos involucrarnos en la guerra y la política; Debemos ser neutrales\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n05/21\n):\n \nJisas ba pulitik lainka ra wapnika mangkaia trai munras kan\n \n–\n \nJesus was not trying to correct (problems) in a\n\npolitical way\n \n/ Jesús no estaba tratando de corregir (problemas) de manera política\n)\n\nPulitik l\nâ\nka\n \n–\n \npolitically\n, way of politics\n \n/ políticamente\n, forma de política\n\nPuno\n \n–\n \ns\nee/ver:\n \nDuarsap\n\nPuntara\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nDuarsap\n\nPupuhkaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nPupuhwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto cause to overflow, to flood, to cause to effervesce, to bubble, to ferment\n \n/\nhacer rebosar, inundar, hacer efervescer, burbujear, fermentar\n\nPupuhwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nPupuhkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto overflow, to flood, to effervesce, to bubble, to ferment\n \n/ rebosar, inundar,\nhacer efervescencia, burbujear, fermentar\n\nPuputni\n \n(a/t:\n \nPuput\n)\n \n–\n \ngray\n \n/ gris\n\nPuputka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngray stain, mold, rust\n \n/ mancha gris, moho, óxido\n\nPur\n \n(\ngpm\n-from English / de inglés) (Alt:\n \nWalhwal\n)\n \n–\n \nfour\n \n/ cuatro\n\nPura\n \n(pos,adv,n/s)\n \n–\n \nup, above, more than, over, high, upper, top, above part, top part\n \n/ arriba, encima, más que, sobre,\nalto, superior, parte superior\n\nPura bikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cover, to hide, to give shelter to, to take in, to cover over\n \n/ cubrir, esconder, dar cobijo, acoger\n\nPura bikaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncovering, lid, someone or something that hides/covers over/takes in/gives shelter to\n \n/\ncubriendo, tapa, alguien o algo que oculta/cubre/toma/da refugio a\n\nPura kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto oversee, to watch over\n \n/ supervisar, vigilar\n\nPura kakaira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \noverseer, administrator, director, supervisor, elder (in the congregation)\n \n/\nsuperintendente, administrador, director, supervisor, anciano (en la congregación)\n\nImpaki pura kakaira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntravelling\n \noverseer, circuit overseer\n \n/\n \nsuperintendente viajante,\n\nsuperintendente de\n \ncircuito\n\nImpaki Pura Kakaira bara ai Maritka nani Skulka\n \n–\n \nSchool for Circuit Overseers and Their\n\nWives\n \n/ Escuela para Superintendentes de Ci\nrcuito y sus Esposas\n\nPura luaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto overcome, to prevail, to conquer\n \n/ vencer, prevalecer, conquistar\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nWan kupia turbanka nani nahki pura luaia?\n \n–\n \nHow do we overcome our anxieties?\n \n/ ¿Cómo superamos nuestras\n\nansiedades?\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nJ\nirimaya\n \n20:7\n):\n \nman... puri luram\n \n–\n \nyou prevailed over me\n \n/ tu prevaleciste sobre mi\n)\n\nPura luan\n \n(adv\n,v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado of/de:\n \nPura luaia\n)\n \n–\n \novercame, prevailed\n, conquered\n \n/ venció,\n\nprevaleció\n, conquistó\n, conquistada\n\nPura luanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nvictory, triumph, conquest, defeat\n \n/ victoria,\n \ntriunfo, conquista, derrota\n\nPura lus\n \n(v\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \novercome, prevail, conquer\n \n/ vence, venza, venzan, prevalece, prevalezca, prevalezcan,\n\nconquista, conquiste, conquisten\n, supere, supera, superen\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYamni l\nâ\nka ba ni saurka ba pura lus\n \n–\n \nOvercome the bad (or evil) with goodness\n \n/ Supera lo malo con\n\nbondad\n)",
